#!/bin/bash
# Cyrus weekly eval gate (deploy/cyrus/cyrus-eval-gate.timer, NOT installed by default). Re-runs the 20-prompt gate
# (scripts/cyrus/eval-gate.ts) against the LIVE build service image and records the verdict on that image's engine release.
# It SPENDS MONEY only when the owner sets CYRUS_EVAL_GATE_BUDGET_USD (e.g. 8) in its environment; unset = a dry run (plan +
# estimate) so installing the timer alone costs nothing. Run from a repo checkout that is NOT /opt/nxeon (REPO, default
# /tank/dev-worktrees/cyrus-eval). Output: /root/cyrus-eval/gate-weekly-<date>/gate.{json,md}.
set -uo pipefail
REPO="${REPO:-/tank/dev-worktrees/cyrus-eval}"
case "$(readlink -f "$REPO")" in /opt/nxeon|/opt/nxeon-staging) echo "refusing to run from a live tree ($REPO)"; exit 2;; esac
cd "$REPO" || { echo "no checkout at $REPO"; exit 2; }
TAG="gate-weekly-$(date -u +%Y%m%d)"
IMAGE="${IMAGE:-$(ssh -o BatchMode=yes -J root@178.63.94.114 root@10.20.1.253 "docker inspect -f '{{.Config.Image}}' modbuilder" 2>/dev/null)}"
TSX="${TSX:-npx tsx}"
if [ -n "${CYRUS_EVAL_GATE_BUDGET_USD:-}" ]; then
  $TSX scripts/cyrus/eval-gate.ts --tag "$TAG" --budget "$CYRUS_EVAL_GATE_BUDGET_USD" --testflight ${IMAGE:+--image "$IMAGE" --record-release}
else
  echo "CYRUS_EVAL_GATE_BUDGET_USD is not set: dry run only (nothing is built or spent)"
  $TSX scripts/cyrus/eval-gate.ts --dry-run --tag "$TAG"
fi
161:## Eval baseline acceptance (rc10)
162-What "accepted" means: a completed eval run (`/root/cyrus-eval/<tag>/`, journal + `baseline.json` + `report.md` written by `scripts/cyrus/eval-run.ts`) that the owner has read and committed as the reference every later gate run is compared with. Without it the gate verdict is `no-reference` (WARN) and `deploy-modbuilder.sh REQUIRE_EVAL_GATE=yes` has nothing to hold an image against.
163-1. **Let the run finish.** `scripts/cyrus/launch-check.sh beta` prints the newest completed run and, separately, a run in progress (`eval-run`, `eval-run-live` rows, read from the journals; no gate.json needed). Do not accept a partial run and do not deploy an image while it runs (the build service must be idle).
164-2. **Read the numbers.** `npx tsx scripts/cyrus/eval-journal-stats.ts /root/cyrus-eval/<tag> --compare /root/cyrus-eval/<previous tag>`: pass@1, final pass, repair share, top repair triggers, failing prompts. Acceptance bar (PLACEHOLDER, owner can change): final pass >= 90%, pass@1 >= 40% (launch check floors `THRESHOLDS.evalMinFinalPassPct`/`evalMinPassAt1Pct`), real boot rate >= 95% of passed builds, no lane with final pass below 80%, no failure class without a named cause.
165-3. **Re-score as a gate run, no spend:** `npx tsx scripts/cyrus/eval-gate.ts --journal /root/cyrus-eval/<tag> --tag accept-<tag>` (writes `gate.json`, schema `cyrus-eval-gate-1`, which the launch check also reads).
166-4. **Accept, in a reviewed branch:** `cp /root/cyrus-eval/<tag>/baseline.json services/modbuilder/eval/baseline.json`, then `npx tsx scripts/cyrus/eval-gate.ts --journal /root/cyrus-eval/<tag> --tag accept-<tag> --accept --accept-recorded` (writes `services/modbuilder/eval/gate-accepted.json`). Commit both files; the commit message names the tag, image and numbers.
167-5. **Verify:** `scripts/cyrus/launch-check.sh beta` shows `eval` and `eval-run` PASS; the weekly timer (`eval-gate-weekly.sh`, needs `CYRUS_EVAL_GATE_BUDGET_USD`) then compares every future image against it.
168-Re-accept after any change that moves quality on purpose (new prompt generation, new sheets); never to hide a regression.
169-
170-## Eval realism: real pass, separate stages, real-world corpus (2026-10-14, branch `feature/cyrus-eval-realism`)
171-Why: a messy real prompt (the goblin creature mod) exposed that the eval headline overstated quality. The plugin lacked `depend: BetterModel` and could not enable, yet the eval's "boot" stage (the Paper server starts) counted it as a pass because nothing required `plugins_enabled`; and the portal could not save the result (`engine.toolchain` over 200 characters), so the build stuck. The old numbers (final pass, pass@1, full pass, boot) are kept everywhere, but they are no longer the headline.
172-
173-**Stages, reported separately** (`lib/cyrus/eval/realpass.ts`; `eval-run` report, `eval-journal-stats`, `baseline.json`, launch-check `eval-run` row): compiled, scanned, server booted (Test Flight `boot`), plugin enabled (`plugins_enabled`), commands registered (`commands_registered`), assets delivered (each planned lane shipped: textures, sounds, designs, data packs, creatures), portal sync ok. Portal sync is checked OFFLINE on every succeeded build (`lib/cyrus/eval/sync-check.ts`): each returned texture/sound/creature/data pack/design goes through the same `checkReturned*` validator the sync uses (an asset the portal would drop is a failure), and the engine record the sync would write goes through `validateEngineRecord`. It does not submit through the real portal path (a dedicated eval user is out of scope); a build the portal cannot save for another reason (DB, store) is not caught here.
174-
175-**Real pass** = built AND plugin ENABLED in the Test Flight AND every planned lane shipped AND portal sync not failing. A build that was not flown is never a real pass (counted as "unverified"): run with `--testflight`, otherwise the real pass is 0 by construction. `real pass@1` = real pass with no model repair. Reports print both, e.g. `REAL pass 61.0%, old final pass 98.3%, old boot 100%`; `real pass` is the number to quote and to gate on.
176-
177-**Compatibility:** `baseline.json` keeps schema `cyrus-eval-baseline-1` and gains optional fields (`realMetrics: 1`, `totals.realPass*`, `results[].realPass/realFirst`); older baselines and journals still load, real pass is then derived from `stages` + `flight.checks` and the portal sync stage reads `not_run`. The gate (`lib/cyrus/eval/gate.ts`) adds `realPassPct`/`realPassAt1Pct` to every metrics block and a `realRegressions` list (a job that was a real pass in the reference and is not now; same limits as final-pass regressions); it only compares real pass when BOTH sides carry it, so an old accepted baseline never fails a run for a field it does not have. Launch check: `eval-run` row shows REAL pass, plugin enabled % of flown, "booted but did NOT enable" and the old numbers; WARN below `THRESHOLDS.evalMinRealPassPct` (75, PLACEHOLDER). Re-accept the baseline from a run that carries real pass before relying on the real regression check.
178-
179-**Failure taxonomy** (`lib/cyrus/eval/taxonomy.ts`, printed by `eval-journal-stats` and in `report.md`): one primary class per build that is not a real pass, ranked: timeout / session limit, budget cap, false refusal, performance guard, compile, safety scan, plugin missing depend / engine class, plugin did not enable (other), design none, texture check, asset check, portal sync / engine record, commands not registered, built but not flown. Infrastructure failures stay out of every rate but appear in the table.
180-
181-**Corpus** `services/modbuilder/eval/real-world-v1.json` (80 messy owner-style prompts; style from the owner's own ModBuild prompts and `scripts/cyrus/qa-owner-batch-prompts.json`, prompt text only): strata creature 30% / GUI-economy-quests 25% / items 20% / datapack-world 10% / admin-minigames 15%; styles short vague, run-on, typos, wrong-genre ("make me a sword", "plugin where goblins steal chests"), chaotic world-changing asks. Each prompt carries `expectLanes`, `expectOutcome` and a `mustHave` (enabled, command and datapack_loaded are verified by the Test Flight today; item_give, mob_summon, gui_open are tagged for a future RCON check and are NOT verified yet). The eval now requests `assets.creature` for `assetKinds: ["creature"]` (new lane `creature`; the old sets never exercised the creature lane, which is where the goblin bug lived). The set is NOT part of `loadEvalSet` (gate subset and python harness stay comparable); presets: `--preset real-world` (80 builds) and `--preset real-world-smoke` (24, stratified 7/6/5/2/4). Always `--dry-run` first: it prints the cost estimate by stratum. Real runs need `--budget` and `--testflight` and an idle build service.
